# LED Mapper — top-level Python dependencies for the whole repo.
#
# Regenerate the locked transitive set with:
#     bazel run //:requirements.update
#
# This file is the only place to add a new direct dependency. The lockfile
# (requirements.lock) is fully resolved from this set and is what Bazel
# actually consumes via pip.parse() in MODULE.bazel.
#
# Per design doc §4, versions are pinned to the latest stable at repo init
# (recorded in docs/decisions.md) and bumped intentionally, not opportunistically.

# Wire-protocol modeling (M10).
pydantic>=2.6
jsonschema>=4.21

# Reconstruction / simulator (M3, M9).
numpy
scipy
opencv-python-headless

# Pi server (M2).
fastapi
uvicorn[standard]
websockets

# Test runner.
pytest

# Bench tooling: pure-Python QR generation for the trace server's pairing
# landing page (tools/trace_server.py). Zero transitive deps.
segno

# Wire protocol (proto-comms branch): protobuf runtime for the generated
# ledmapper.v1 bindings.
protobuf==6.33.5

# Build tooling: template expansion behind //tools/jinja:jinja_template
# (bakes build constants into shipped resources with StrictUndefined).
jinja2

# Host-side hardware-test drivers (run on the machine with the board + BT radio;
# see tools/ble_onboard_server.py + tools/browser_server.py). SimpleBLE drives
# the Improv-BLE onboarding; Playwright drives headless Chromium for the wss/cert
# flow (the browser binary installs separately: `playwright install chromium`).
simplepyble
playwright

# Algorithmic place-and-route engine (FUG-138). The differentiable placement
# core (DREAMPlace/Cypress-style: LSE wirelength + density + net-crossing) is a
# PyTorch autograd program — see docs/hardware/pnr-system.md §4/§8. CPU-first by
# design (determinism + no GPU in CI).
#
# The `<2.4` ceiling keeps the lockfile CPU-only and cross-platform: from 2.4 on,
# PyTorch ships CUDA-enabled aarch64 (sbsa) wheels, so resolving on this aarch64
# host would drag ~20 linux-only `nvidia-*`/`triton` wheels into the single,
# markerless requirements.lock — which then fails to resolve on macOS-arm64 (dev)
# where those wheels don't exist. Under 2.4 the aarch64 wheel is CPU-only and the
# x86_64 nvidia deps are platform-marked, so an aarch64 resolve drops them. pyyaml
# parses the sidecar constraints.yaml (§3).
torch>=2.2,<2.4
pyyaml>=6

# Developer documentation (FUG-104). Sphinx site generated by //docs:build:
# MyST folds the existing markdown in as-is; furo is the theme; copybutton +
# design + mermaid are presentation extensions; matplotlib renders the generated
# fixture/reconstruction figures and animations. See docs/ and docs/decisions.md.
sphinx
myst-parser
furo
sphinx-copybutton
sphinx-design
sphinxcontrib-mermaid
matplotlib
